{"id": "EUVD-2026-27688", "enisaUuid": "88e1826b-e6b7-3185-8670-76223df440ae", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\ndlm: validate length in dlm_search_rsb_tree\n\nThe len parameter in dlm_dump_rsb_name() is not validated and comes\nfrom network messages. When it exceeds DLM_RESNAME_MAXLEN, it can\ncause out-of-bounds write in dlm_search_rsb_tree().\n\nAdd length validation to prevent potential buffer overflow.", "datePublished": "2026-05-06T11:27:10", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:40:07", "baseScore": 9.8, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:H/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2deafd015ea9a0e75ee5764e20eb1e16bd73efd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/67288113c5e6cf9e659b4065c0ed6f16100e0c71", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/082083c9fbd99422a0370fe2102144a231c9f5d6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5f053a2e7209d326cbbc07738fa6d6893d307438", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/080e5563f878c64e697b89e7439d730d0daad882"], "aliases": ["GHSA-fr2c-799q-pg3x", "CVE-2026-43125"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.43, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "02134734-5b05-3645-919b-a8cf5fe2ef48", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7210cb7a72a22303cdb225bd1aea28697a17bbae <2deafd015ea9a0e75ee5764e20eb1e16bd73efd8"}, {"id": "13dbc33d-3c4f-3df1-b95d-a069ad4c0dc1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7210cb7a72a22303cdb225bd1aea28697a17bbae <080e5563f878c64e697b89e7439d730d0daad882"}, {"id": "28b30447-1733-3c5b-abba-8eacc33dc844", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "7210cb7a72a22303cdb225bd1aea28697a17bbae <5f053a2e7209d326cbbc07738fa6d6893d307438"}, {"id": "2b038aa3-e30f-3b44-aa23-a5ac38a29dae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.75"}, {"id": "2c4893b8-a353-378a-ba98-e24949378963", "product": {"